agent	Parse MCP Gateway logs for step summary	2026-10-20T07:11:59.5089416Z {"timestamp":"2026-10-20T07:11:51.033Z","event":"rpc_request","_schema":"rpc-message/v2","direction":"OUT","server_id":"safeoutputs","method":"tools/call","payload":{"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"tools/call","params":{"arguments":{"body":"Thanks for the report! This is an automated first-pass triage; a maintainer will make the final call.\n\n**Reproduction:**\n- Black 25.1.1: not run. That release postdates nothing the tooling could pin here, and it is likely the playground's dev build string.\n- Black 25.11.0 (latest on the issue date), default flags, snippet from the report: crash (`INTERNAL ERROR: ... produced code that is not equivalent to the source`).\n\n**Assessment:** The crash reproduces on the latest release with the snippet you gave. The trigger looks like the two trailing \"ignore\" comments (`# pyright: ignore[...]` and `# type: ignore[operator]`) in the same expression. Black appears to drop or mishandle the `type: ignore` comment, so the AST differs.\n\n**Next step:** A maintainer can confirm. If you can, try shrinking the snippet to the smallest input that still fails, for example by removing the pandas parts. See the comment handling in the style docs: https://black.readthedocs.io/en/stable/the_black_code_style/current_style.html#comments\n\n\u003csub\u003eblack-issue-triage skill v1.0.0 · suggested for maintainers: none\u003c/sub\u003e"},"name":"add_comment"}}}
